OL,3,GNEWSAMillionaire who abused women in
OL,4,AHighland home loses travel ban appeal
OL,5,
OL,6,FA millionaire who abused vulnerable
OL,7,Fwomen in his Highland lodge has lost an
OL,8,Fappeal to overturn a worldwide travel
OL,9,Fban.
OL,11,FIn February 2025, a civil court ruled
OL,12,Fthat Kevin Booth recruited women from
OL,13,Fthe UK and abroad and submitted them to
OL,14,Fviolent beatings at his home in a
OL,15,Fremote area of Caithness.
OL,17,FHe was given a ban preventing him from
OL,18,Ftravelling outside the UK for five
OL,19,Fyears after Police Scotland raised the
OL,20,Fcivil action against him. It was the
OL,21,Ffirst worldwide travel ban to be
OL,22,Fimposed by a Scottish court.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
